1
00:00:44,339 --> 00:00:48,969
DEAR X

2
00:00:49,845 --> 00:00:51,889
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES, AND EVENTS
IN THIS WORK ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:51,972 --> 00:00:53,515
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

4
00:02:04,878 --> 00:02:06,130
Two, three. Clear!

5
00:02:15,055 --> 00:02:17,724
CARDIAC PACEMAKER

6
00:02:44,751 --> 00:02:46,253
- One, two, three. Clear!
- At that fork

7
00:02:47,129 --> 00:02:49,631
where one life stands
between life and death

8
00:02:51,758 --> 00:02:53,886
what kind of prayer
did desperate Ah-jin

9
00:02:55,554 --> 00:02:57,055
offer up?

10
00:02:59,558 --> 00:03:01,018
At death's door

11
00:03:02,394 --> 00:03:04,021
was that one's life

12
00:03:05,606 --> 00:03:06,607
or one's end?

13
00:03:19,286 --> 00:03:20,287
Was that death

14
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:24,499
God's answer to Ah-jin's prayer

15
00:03:26,293 --> 00:03:27,294
or His punishment?

16
00:03:42,434 --> 00:03:43,435
WITH DEEPEST CONDOLENCES

17
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,161
No!

18
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,588
Grandma!

19
00:05:20,699 --> 00:05:25,620
EPISODE 8: BEFORE JUDGMENT

20
00:05:28,415 --> 00:05:30,959
SAMYUN SEOUL HOSPITAL MEMORIAL HALL

21
00:05:31,043 --> 00:05:33,462
NOTICE REGARDING MEDIA COVERAGE

22
00:06:27,182 --> 00:06:29,559
REST IN PEACE

23
00:06:33,772 --> 00:06:34,898
Get some rest.

24
00:06:34,981 --> 00:06:36,483
You'll collapse at this rate.

25
00:06:36,566 --> 00:06:38,318
I'll take him outside for a moment.

26
00:06:41,571 --> 00:06:43,365
HONG KYUNG-SUK

27
00:06:50,831 --> 00:06:52,874
- You two know each other?
- Yes.

28
00:06:52,958 --> 00:06:54,709
He helped me out a lot.

29
00:06:54,793 --> 00:06:57,587
And I worked part-time
at his café for a year.

30
00:07:01,675 --> 00:07:05,804
BASEBALL PLAYER CHOI ARRESTED
FOR MURDERING A PART-TIMER'S FATHER

31
00:07:05,887 --> 00:07:08,140
PARTIALLY ADMITTED GUILT
AND SAID "IT WAS IMPULSIVE"

32
00:07:20,694 --> 00:07:22,821
I was going to go home

33
00:07:24,156 --> 00:07:25,490
after In-gang left.

34
00:07:27,242 --> 00:07:28,910
But I went to her place instead.

35
00:07:31,288 --> 00:07:33,081
He had asked me

36
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:39,796
and I remembered she hasn't been
sleeping well at night lately.

37
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:44,551
I wanted to keep her company.

38
00:07:44,634 --> 00:07:47,804
I thought of you
as a gift from my daughter.

39
00:07:49,723 --> 00:07:53,310
I scolded In-gang for doubting you
and pushing you away.

40
00:07:54,811 --> 00:07:56,521
I reprimanded him for that.

41
00:07:57,439 --> 00:08:00,775
You looked so pitiful
when I first saw you

42
00:08:00,859 --> 00:08:03,111
so I believed
you could never do such a thing.

43
00:08:03,862 --> 00:08:04,863
The one who deceived me...

44
00:08:05,489 --> 00:08:06,490
No.

45
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:08,950
The one who deceived my whole family!

46
00:08:10,118 --> 00:08:11,912
I foolishly trusted you

47
00:08:12,662 --> 00:08:15,624
and I drove my own grandson...

48
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:19,628
into a bottomless pit.

49
00:08:25,967 --> 00:08:26,968
What...

50
00:08:27,886 --> 00:08:29,346
What should I do?

51
00:08:31,181 --> 00:08:33,558
What am I supposed to do now, Ah-jin?

52
00:08:35,852 --> 00:08:38,980
Can you explain what happened

53
00:08:39,064 --> 00:08:41,566
before and after the fall?

54
00:08:46,446 --> 00:08:47,656
A cat.

55
00:08:50,033 --> 00:08:51,993
She went out to show me

56
00:08:53,495 --> 00:08:56,498
the kitten that had come by.

57
00:08:57,999 --> 00:08:59,000
A cat?

58
00:09:01,378 --> 00:09:02,587
She used to feed

59
00:09:03,922 --> 00:09:06,925
the stray cats in the neighborhood.

60
00:09:07,175 --> 00:09:11,263
In-mo is allergic,
so she couldn't let them inside.

61
00:09:14,015 --> 00:09:17,060
She had only put food out for them.

62
00:09:18,353 --> 00:09:22,357
Sometimes, the cats would bring
their kittens

63
00:09:22,983 --> 00:09:24,234
and show up at her door

64
00:09:25,485 --> 00:09:27,362
at night.

65
00:09:28,071 --> 00:09:29,072
Please continue.

66
00:09:30,532 --> 00:09:32,617
After putting food out for them...

67
00:09:34,953 --> 00:09:36,288
she was standing up...

68
00:09:38,498 --> 00:09:42,335
when she suddenly swayed
as if she got dizzy.

69
00:09:52,929 --> 00:09:54,472
Then, she lost consciousness.

70
00:10:01,438 --> 00:10:02,439
I see.

71
00:10:03,356 --> 00:10:05,150
I know this is hard

72
00:10:06,568 --> 00:10:08,236
but I have a few more questions.

73
00:10:27,714 --> 00:10:28,798
I'll take care of it.

74
00:10:29,633 --> 00:10:31,843
I'll wipe every security camera
and dash cam clean

75
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:34,679
so get her away from here.

76
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,182
It's more natural
to say that I was here.

77
00:10:39,184 --> 00:10:40,894
And there aren't
any security cameras here.

78
00:10:42,562 --> 00:10:43,813
Don't do anything stupid.

79
00:10:58,578 --> 00:11:01,331
A grandma fell down the stairs.

80
00:11:03,625 --> 00:11:04,751
Please hurry.

81
00:11:15,804 --> 00:11:16,805
Wait!

82
00:11:20,058 --> 00:11:22,519
I'd like to know
exactly what kind of relationship

83
00:11:22,936 --> 00:11:24,229
you have with Baek Ah-jin.

84
00:11:24,604 --> 00:11:25,772
I looked you up.

85
00:11:26,147 --> 00:11:28,024
The Nojeong-dong Rooftop Murder Case.

86
00:11:28,650 --> 00:11:31,528
What does that have to do
with Dharma Sister Yeonhwa's passing?

87
00:11:31,611 --> 00:11:33,363
I read that you testified
you were caught in a trap

88
00:11:33,446 --> 00:11:35,949
set by the victim's daughter,
who worked part-time at your café.

89
00:11:36,032 --> 00:11:38,034
What exactly are you trying to ask?

90
00:11:38,952 --> 00:11:41,621
Is it whether there's a link

91
00:11:41,705 --> 00:11:43,790
between Baek Ah-jin
and her father's murder?

92
00:11:43,873 --> 00:11:45,166
Can you answer that?

93
00:11:45,917 --> 00:11:47,210
You want an answer?

94
00:11:51,881 --> 00:11:53,967
Between the murder
of Mr. Baek Seon-gyu...

95
00:11:56,094 --> 00:11:57,804
and Ms. Baek Ah-jin...

96
00:12:01,975 --> 00:12:02,976
there is no connection.

97
00:12:03,852 --> 00:12:04,853
Sorry?

98
00:12:04,936 --> 00:12:06,479
No connection whatsoever.

99
00:12:07,313 --> 00:12:10,024
Back then, I testified like that
out of a cowardly wish

100
00:12:10,108 --> 00:12:12,861
to slip through the law
because I was afraid

101
00:12:12,944 --> 00:12:14,362
of becoming a criminal.

102
00:12:15,405 --> 00:12:16,906
Which I regret now.

103
00:12:18,199 --> 00:12:22,078
I served five years
and paid for my crime behind bars

104
00:12:22,871 --> 00:12:24,372
but my debt to the deceased

105
00:12:25,623 --> 00:12:27,584
is something I must carry for life.

106
00:12:30,211 --> 00:12:31,296
Baek Ah-jin is

107
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:34,966
simply a bereaved daughter
who lost her family.

108
00:12:35,049 --> 00:12:36,259
She's someone

109
00:12:37,093 --> 00:12:38,887
I must keep apologizing to
until the day I die.

110
00:12:39,512 --> 00:12:41,723
Since she became so famous

111
00:12:42,515 --> 00:12:45,935
there will inevitably be
all kinds of rumors.

112
00:12:46,019 --> 00:12:47,937
But they're baseless.

113
00:12:48,605 --> 00:12:49,606
I'm relieved to hear that.

114
00:12:50,398 --> 00:12:51,858
Thank you for coming.

115
00:13:01,618 --> 00:13:03,369
Why did you tell him that?

116
00:13:10,835 --> 00:13:12,212
It was a chance to get revenge.

117
00:13:15,757 --> 00:13:17,050
Why defend me?

118
00:13:23,807 --> 00:13:25,350
During my first year in prison...

119
00:13:27,894 --> 00:13:29,604
I wondered what I'd do to you

120
00:13:31,105 --> 00:13:32,565
once I got out...

121
00:13:34,734 --> 00:13:35,985
and how to pay you back.

122
00:13:38,321 --> 00:13:39,447
During the second year

123
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:42,367
I kept thinking...

124
00:13:44,828 --> 00:13:46,037
"Why me, of all people?"

125
00:13:48,748 --> 00:13:50,625
After the third winter...

126
00:13:53,253 --> 00:13:55,755
I started thinking
about what could have driven you...

127
00:13:58,383 --> 00:14:00,051
to do something so horrific.

128
00:14:02,178 --> 00:14:03,513
And the year after that...

129
00:14:06,516 --> 00:14:08,518
I began taking pity on you.

130
00:14:11,479 --> 00:14:14,649
If you had had
even one proper adult in your life

131
00:14:16,192 --> 00:14:17,861
as a child

132
00:14:18,444 --> 00:14:22,740
I thought your path
might have been different.

133
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:25,910
So, in the last year

134
00:14:28,079 --> 00:14:29,414
I decided to pray for you.

135
00:14:31,624 --> 00:14:33,042
And I started wondering

136
00:14:33,918 --> 00:14:37,797
if I could become
that one adult for you.

137
00:14:41,342 --> 00:14:42,969
Once I thought about it that way

138
00:14:44,721 --> 00:14:46,556
I stopped resenting you.

139
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,643
So, don't carry any guilt.

140
00:14:52,604 --> 00:14:53,646
What happened then

141
00:14:55,106 --> 00:14:56,649
was simply my fate.

142
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:00,361
That sounds just like you.

143
00:15:01,571 --> 00:15:03,156
I'm going to root for you.

144
00:15:03,698 --> 00:15:04,824
That's my way.

145
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:11,831
So, live your life
remembering there's someone out there

146
00:15:12,498 --> 00:15:15,335
who genuinely pities you

147
00:15:17,629 --> 00:15:18,880
and sincerely cheers for you.

148
00:15:21,507 --> 00:15:22,800
Try living like that.

149
00:15:26,679 --> 00:15:28,598
That's the best revenge I can offer.

150
00:15:34,771 --> 00:15:37,106
But Mr. Choi.

151
00:15:42,070 --> 00:15:44,322
There's no such thing
as "best revenge."

152
00:15:46,115 --> 00:15:47,617
What just happened was

153
00:15:48,576 --> 00:15:50,578
that you missed
your one and only chance

154
00:15:51,621 --> 00:15:53,623
to take revenge on me.

155
00:15:59,045 --> 00:16:00,046
Thank you.

156
00:16:10,098 --> 00:16:11,641
HEO IN-GANG WAS KNOWN
TO BE DEEPLY AFFECTIONATE

157
00:16:11,724 --> 00:16:13,101
TOWARD HIS GRANDMOTHER...

158
00:16:13,184 --> 00:16:14,894
Baek Ah-jin and Heo In-gang?

159
00:16:15,353 --> 00:16:17,480
How long are you going to milk them?

160
00:16:17,563 --> 00:16:18,898
It works for the public.

161
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:20,775
They're like a bone broth.

162
00:16:20,858 --> 00:16:23,277
You boil and boil,
and it still gives.

163
00:16:23,361 --> 00:16:26,239
It's about time
they broke up, though.

164
00:16:26,781 --> 00:16:29,075
I was going to lock in the breakup
as an exclusive

165
00:16:29,158 --> 00:16:30,660
and be done with it.

166
00:16:30,743 --> 00:16:32,829
Why split up a couple
that's doing fine?

167
00:16:32,912 --> 00:16:34,622
Isn't it obvious?

168
00:16:35,039 --> 00:16:37,542
Ah-jin is a rising sun,
and In-gang is a setting sun.

169
00:16:38,084 --> 00:16:41,754
She's gotten everything
she could out of him.

170
00:16:41,838 --> 00:16:44,424
Why would she keep dating him?

171
00:16:44,507 --> 00:16:46,300
Who knows?

172
00:16:46,384 --> 00:16:47,552
It could be true love.

173
00:16:50,847 --> 00:16:53,933
"True love"? You don't know anything.

174
00:17:22,211 --> 00:17:23,671
What do you want?

175
00:17:23,755 --> 00:17:25,006
Oh, nothing.

176
00:17:25,089 --> 00:17:28,801
I'm just calling to see
if there's anything new.

177
00:17:28,885 --> 00:17:32,597
Nothing pulls clicks
like you and In-gang.

178
00:17:33,056 --> 00:17:35,391
We're in mourning. Show some respect.

179
00:17:35,475 --> 00:17:37,143
I have something to verify--

180
00:17:37,226 --> 00:17:38,227
Hello?

181
00:17:38,644 --> 00:17:39,645
Hello...

182
00:17:42,023 --> 00:17:43,483
Right.

183
00:17:44,358 --> 00:17:46,277
For a time like this...

184
00:17:48,071 --> 00:17:49,072
RÉSUMÉ

185
00:17:49,155 --> 00:17:50,364
PHOTO

186
00:17:51,324 --> 00:17:53,159
Hello, Ms. Sim Sung-hee?

187
00:17:53,576 --> 00:17:55,286
I told you I never did that.

188
00:17:55,369 --> 00:17:57,914
It looks like Ah-jin's side
has already made a move.

189
00:17:57,997 --> 00:17:59,665
Was it Longstar's CEO, Seo Mi-ri?

190
00:18:00,124 --> 00:18:01,667
I don't know
what you're talking about.

191
00:18:02,877 --> 00:18:05,171
If you're going to keep talking
nonsense, I'm hanging up.

192
00:18:13,054 --> 00:18:14,680
I did what you told me to.

193
00:18:15,348 --> 00:18:16,599
Guess you're scared, after all.

194
00:18:20,269 --> 00:18:21,270
Figures.

195
00:18:21,646 --> 00:18:24,398
Your dad's past
as an adulterous lawyer

196
00:18:24,690 --> 00:18:27,151
and your own past,
stealing your classmates' stuff

197
00:18:27,235 --> 00:18:29,028
beaten by the homeroom teacher
and kids

198
00:18:29,112 --> 00:18:30,655
and forced to transfer.

199
00:18:31,906 --> 00:18:34,200
It'll look bad on you
if those spread in your workplace.

200
00:18:37,036 --> 00:18:39,539
You saw the comments
on your post last time, right?

201
00:18:40,832 --> 00:18:42,667
Plenty of people still remember you.

202
00:18:43,459 --> 00:18:46,003
So, unless you want
your past dragged out in the open

203
00:18:46,087 --> 00:18:47,588
shut your mouth and lie low.

204
00:18:51,134 --> 00:18:52,135
If not

205
00:18:53,427 --> 00:18:55,972
I'll follow you around
with your past everywhere you go.

206
00:19:07,483 --> 00:19:08,484
Fuck.

207
00:19:08,568 --> 00:19:11,863
SAMYUN SEOUL HOSPITAL MEMORIAL HALL

208
00:19:14,907 --> 00:19:15,908
Director.

209
00:19:18,077 --> 00:19:19,078
Hello.

210
00:19:21,247 --> 00:19:22,665
Are you heading out now?

211
00:19:23,082 --> 00:19:24,667
Oh, Ms. Baek Ah-jin.

212
00:19:25,793 --> 00:19:27,503
I'm glad you know my name.

213
00:19:27,587 --> 00:19:29,338
I was nervous you might not.

214
00:19:29,589 --> 00:19:32,091
Of course, I do.
I enjoyed your works.

215
00:19:32,633 --> 00:19:33,634
Thank you.

216
00:19:34,552 --> 00:19:36,804
I've watched all of yours as well.

217
00:19:37,054 --> 00:19:38,681
I'm a big fan.

218
00:19:38,764 --> 00:19:40,892
And In-gang talks about you so much.

219
00:19:40,975 --> 00:19:44,353
He does?
I should buy him a meal sometime.

220
00:19:44,437 --> 00:19:45,438
No need.

221
00:19:45,938 --> 00:19:47,815
Since you came today

222
00:19:47,899 --> 00:19:53,654
once he settles down,
let me treat you to a meal with him.

223
00:19:55,072 --> 00:19:56,282
What do you say?

224
00:19:56,532 --> 00:19:58,409
I'd love that. Anytime.

225
00:19:59,118 --> 00:20:00,953
For today, please stay by him

226
00:20:01,537 --> 00:20:02,955
and comfort him.

227
00:20:03,789 --> 00:20:04,790
I will.

228
00:20:06,667 --> 00:20:08,753
- Get home safe.
- Thanks.

229
00:20:12,423 --> 00:20:13,507
Ms. Baek.

230
00:20:15,343 --> 00:20:17,053
If you don't mind

231
00:20:17,136 --> 00:20:19,639
how about you drop
by my studio sometime?

232
00:20:23,726 --> 00:20:26,604
He must have seen Ah-jin
at In-gang's grandma's funeral.

233
00:20:26,854 --> 00:20:28,606
He said she was the image
he'd been looking for

234
00:20:28,689 --> 00:20:32,985
and wants her to play
a key role in his new work.

235
00:20:33,486 --> 00:20:35,279
Director Seol Yeong-uk is...

236
00:20:35,363 --> 00:20:37,156
It'll be invited
to the Cannes Film Festival

237
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:39,784
and that naturally opens
a route into the global market.

238
00:20:39,867 --> 00:20:42,161
There's no better opportunity
for an actor.

239
00:20:42,245 --> 00:20:44,413
It's what every actor dreams of.

240
00:20:47,583 --> 00:20:51,045
In-gang's grandma left Ah-jin
a big gift as she passed.

241
00:21:09,981 --> 00:21:11,399
You're curious, aren't you?

242
00:21:12,275 --> 00:21:15,403
Whether I was the one
who did it to her that night.

243
00:21:23,119 --> 00:21:24,495
What do you think?

244
00:21:26,038 --> 00:21:28,040
Do you think I could go that far?

245
00:21:33,004 --> 00:21:34,171
I don't get you.

246
00:21:38,509 --> 00:21:40,094
It must have been hard

247
00:21:40,344 --> 00:21:42,888
thinking about what to do with a girl
who even committed a murder.

248
00:21:44,223 --> 00:21:45,224
Say it.

249
00:21:47,727 --> 00:21:49,145
It wasn't you, right?

250
00:21:49,228 --> 00:21:51,689
And what happens if it were me?

251
00:21:57,361 --> 00:21:58,446
You're right.

252
00:22:00,114 --> 00:22:01,782
She started getting on my nerves.

253
00:22:02,783 --> 00:22:04,660
She was no use to me anymore

254
00:22:05,369 --> 00:22:07,079
and constantly got in my way.

255
00:22:08,998 --> 00:22:11,792
She had also found out
that I approached her on purpose.

256
00:22:15,796 --> 00:22:19,425
So, what do you think I did to her?

257
00:22:21,052 --> 00:22:22,053
Is that true?

258
00:22:22,511 --> 00:22:23,804
Did you really do it?

259
00:22:25,264 --> 00:22:26,974
Whatever you're thinking
is the truth.

260
00:22:27,058 --> 00:22:28,059
Baek Ah-jin.

261
00:22:34,565 --> 00:22:36,108
This is so exhausting.

262
00:23:29,578 --> 00:23:31,414
Excuse me.

263
00:23:31,831 --> 00:23:34,583
You're the grandson of the lady
who lived in Unit 401, right?

264
00:23:38,170 --> 00:23:40,005
My grandma was crying?

265
00:23:40,589 --> 00:23:44,093
Yes, she was practically wailing,
so I was shocked.

266
00:23:44,176 --> 00:23:45,636
She normally doesn't do that.

267
00:23:46,137 --> 00:23:48,097
By the time she calmed down

268
00:23:48,180 --> 00:23:50,933
a pretty, young woman
walked into her place.

269
00:23:51,225 --> 00:23:54,311
I brought her some red bean porridge

270
00:23:54,562 --> 00:23:56,689
and saw something strange
at the door.

271
00:23:57,982 --> 00:23:59,066
What was it?

272
00:23:59,150 --> 00:24:02,570
Your grandma was pounding
the young woman's chest

273
00:24:02,987 --> 00:24:07,199
saying things like, "I trusted you
who deceived my whole family."

274
00:24:07,283 --> 00:24:09,368
It was something like that.

275
00:24:11,912 --> 00:24:15,374
Also, the woman in Unit 409 said

276
00:24:15,458 --> 00:24:17,334
someone kept stealing her packages

277
00:24:17,418 --> 00:24:20,296
so she secretly set up
a camera in the hallway.

278
00:24:21,255 --> 00:24:23,799
But it's illegal

279
00:24:23,883 --> 00:24:26,177
so she probably didn't tell
the police.

280
00:24:26,260 --> 00:24:28,596
But if your grandma fell
down the stairs

281
00:24:28,679 --> 00:24:30,389
between the fourth and third floors

282
00:24:30,473 --> 00:24:32,516
it might have been filmed.

283
00:24:34,977 --> 00:24:38,022
Could I speak with her?

284
00:24:38,731 --> 00:24:41,775
My husband saved
a copy of the footage just in case

285
00:24:41,859 --> 00:24:43,527
but a detective came and got it.

286
00:24:44,069 --> 00:24:45,696
I see.

287
00:24:46,530 --> 00:24:47,573
Thank you.

288
00:25:06,133 --> 00:25:07,760
Don't ever make me do
stuff like this again.

289
00:25:08,427 --> 00:25:11,096
You, of all people,
should believe in Ah-jin, damn it.

290
00:25:13,140 --> 00:25:14,767
- Did you see it?
- No.

291
00:25:15,392 --> 00:25:16,435
I don't need to.

292
00:25:16,894 --> 00:25:18,437
I believe her. She's innocent.

293
00:25:28,364 --> 00:25:29,782
And don't worry about Sung-hee.

294
00:25:30,366 --> 00:25:32,826
I gave her a good scare, so she won't
dare open her mouth again.

295
00:25:32,910 --> 00:25:34,453
She won't be spreading stories
about Ah-jin.

296
00:25:35,287 --> 00:25:36,288
Good.

297
00:26:04,483 --> 00:26:06,819
In-gang, are you still in bed?

298
00:26:06,902 --> 00:26:08,153
Yes, why?

299
00:26:08,612 --> 00:26:10,531
Come on. You too?

300
00:26:11,532 --> 00:26:13,784
I heard you backed out of the film
you were supposed to do.

301
00:26:14,618 --> 00:26:16,912
We've got to hang in there
now more than ever.

302
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:19,039
Don't keep starving yourself.

303
00:26:19,790 --> 00:26:21,250
Remember to eat.

304
00:26:22,459 --> 00:26:24,295
Ah-jin brought me some porridge.

305
00:26:25,462 --> 00:26:26,589
I'll have it later.

306
00:26:45,274 --> 00:26:47,818
I saw you were asleep, so I left.

307
00:26:47,901 --> 00:26:49,778
Don't skip meals, okay?

308
00:26:50,487 --> 00:26:51,530
I love you.

309
00:26:55,868 --> 00:26:57,202
HEO IN-GANG SPOTTED
SHOPPING FOR RINGS IN HONG KONG

310
00:26:58,078 --> 00:27:01,165
There are headlines saying
you're about to get married now.

311
00:27:01,248 --> 00:27:03,042
This is a problem, Ms. Baek.

312
00:27:03,292 --> 00:27:05,002
You do know

313
00:27:05,085 --> 00:27:07,338
what kind of character
you're playing, right?

314
00:27:07,421 --> 00:27:10,424
If audiences can't stay
immersed in my film

315
00:27:10,507 --> 00:27:13,802
because of your real-life romance
or marriage rumors

316
00:27:13,886 --> 00:27:16,096
I've got no reason to cast you, do I?

317
00:27:17,556 --> 00:27:18,557
I'm sorry.

318
00:27:19,266 --> 00:27:21,894
I wasn't expecting
this kind of speculation, either.

319
00:27:25,898 --> 00:27:29,485
I actually like
seeing you and In-gang together.

320
00:27:29,568 --> 00:27:33,739
I got to work with you thanks to him,
and I appreciate that.

321
00:27:33,822 --> 00:27:36,575
But let's keep personal
and professional matters separate.

322
00:27:36,659 --> 00:27:38,619
You're not dumb enough
to confuse them

323
00:27:39,453 --> 00:27:40,454
right?

324
00:27:41,622 --> 00:27:42,623
No, Director.

325
00:27:44,208 --> 00:27:46,043
Director, you're already here!

326
00:27:46,126 --> 00:27:47,586
I came as early as I could.

327
00:27:48,587 --> 00:27:50,339
Long time no see, Ms. Seo.

328
00:27:50,631 --> 00:27:51,632
Hi.

329
00:27:53,592 --> 00:27:56,345
I don't see Mr. Yoon, though.
Is he running late?

330
00:27:57,179 --> 00:28:00,349
He said
we should meet on a better day.

331
00:28:01,058 --> 00:28:03,560
He said today wasn't
the night for drinking.

332
00:28:04,687 --> 00:28:08,607
Anyway, I'll get going.
Let's talk again soon.

333
00:28:09,358 --> 00:28:10,484
Of course.

334
00:28:10,859 --> 00:28:12,069
We'll see you soon.

335
00:28:12,569 --> 00:28:13,779
Take care!

336
00:28:20,828 --> 00:28:23,038
It must have been tough
cleaning up the mess.

337
00:28:24,123 --> 00:28:26,834
I only posted a statement asking
to refrain from wild speculations.

338
00:28:27,459 --> 00:28:28,502
What about In-gang?

339
00:28:29,586 --> 00:28:31,922
When has he ever cared
about articles?

340
00:28:32,381 --> 00:28:34,925
His fans are already freaking out
that he can't get married yet.

341
00:28:35,592 --> 00:28:37,469
But he's talking about retiring
once his contract's over.

342
00:28:37,553 --> 00:28:38,971
It's driving me insane.

343
00:28:42,015 --> 00:28:43,934
He really said that?

344
00:28:45,728 --> 00:28:47,146
He didn't tell you?

345
00:28:47,646 --> 00:28:49,606
I had my phone turned off.

346
00:28:50,566 --> 00:28:52,818
It was getting too chaotic
due to all the calls coming in.

347
00:28:56,822 --> 00:28:59,533
You didn't know
about the ring, either, did you?

348
00:29:01,118 --> 00:29:02,119
No.

349
00:29:03,996 --> 00:29:06,039
Are you going to marry him?

350
00:29:11,295 --> 00:29:13,297
No, I'm going to end it.

351
00:29:14,506 --> 00:29:15,883
You'll back me up, right?

352
00:29:18,343 --> 00:29:19,344
Ah-jin.

353
00:29:19,970 --> 00:29:21,638
While preparing for your birthday

354
00:29:22,806 --> 00:29:24,808
I realized

355
00:29:24,892 --> 00:29:27,227
it was the first time in my life
I had ever felt so deeply grateful

356
00:29:27,895 --> 00:29:29,021
that someone was born.

357
00:29:30,189 --> 00:29:35,277
I suddenly understood how huge
my feelings for you had become.

358
00:29:36,695 --> 00:29:37,946
This must be love.

359
00:29:39,740 --> 00:29:41,700
Let's share our lives together.

360
00:29:43,243 --> 00:29:45,996
Let's fill and exchange our love

361
00:29:46,830 --> 00:29:48,040
within the same everyday life.

362
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:50,793
I want to marry you.

363
00:29:52,377 --> 00:29:53,504
You're home, right?

364
00:30:05,891 --> 00:30:08,185
I'll be at your place in ten minutes.

365
00:30:08,727 --> 00:30:09,728
We need to talk.

366
00:30:13,482 --> 00:30:15,400
Will you stay by my side?

367
00:30:35,295 --> 00:30:36,505
What are you hesitating about?

368
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:38,173
Is it something exciting?

369
00:30:39,508 --> 00:30:40,592
Something scary.

370
00:30:40,843 --> 00:30:42,761
I'm not sure if I can handle it.

371
00:30:42,845 --> 00:30:43,887
Scary?

372
00:30:44,263 --> 00:30:45,264
Like what?

373
00:30:46,056 --> 00:30:47,266
It's just scary.

374
00:30:49,768 --> 00:30:51,353
Then throw it away.

375
00:30:51,436 --> 00:30:52,646
I wish I could.

376
00:30:58,902 --> 00:31:01,113
Why isn't he home yet?

377
00:31:06,743 --> 00:31:07,870
Man.

378
00:31:09,496 --> 00:31:10,497
What are you doing?

379
00:31:11,665 --> 00:31:13,208
Wait, who are you?

380
00:31:13,917 --> 00:31:14,918
"Who are you?"

381
00:31:15,002 --> 00:31:16,003
Are you serious?

382
00:31:16,545 --> 00:31:18,964
Don't you even remember the guy
you hugged last time?

383
00:31:20,883 --> 00:31:22,175
Go make some ramyeon.

384
00:31:22,801 --> 00:31:23,802
I'm sorry?

385
00:31:25,888 --> 00:31:27,681
It's for Jun-seo's stomach.

386
00:31:28,473 --> 00:31:30,767
He needs something spicy to sober up.

387
00:31:34,104 --> 00:31:35,647
Jackass.

388
00:31:55,167 --> 00:31:56,168
Gosh.

389
00:32:20,943 --> 00:32:23,403
I was worried
something had happened to you.

390
00:32:25,238 --> 00:32:26,865
It relieves me to see your face.

391
00:32:30,577 --> 00:32:33,789
In-gang,
are you thinking of retiring?

392
00:32:36,416 --> 00:32:37,668
Did Mi-ri tell you?

393
00:32:39,252 --> 00:32:41,630
Why didn't you tell me first?

394
00:32:42,547 --> 00:32:44,174
I didn't mean to hide it.

395
00:32:45,050 --> 00:32:47,302
It wasn't easy to make up my mind.

396
00:32:47,678 --> 00:32:50,555
I was going to tell you
once I was sure.

397
00:32:59,064 --> 00:33:03,276
Are you planning to marry me
after you retire?

398
00:33:08,156 --> 00:33:09,908
I thought we were on the same page.

399
00:33:11,952 --> 00:33:13,078
Was I wrong?

400
00:33:14,913 --> 00:33:17,624
Then you shouldn't have let it
become news.

401
00:33:18,250 --> 00:33:19,292
What?

402
00:33:22,754 --> 00:33:24,715
I feel awful.

403
00:33:26,466 --> 00:33:27,592
Do you have any idea

404
00:33:27,676 --> 00:33:29,553
how humiliated I was
in front of the director today?

405
00:33:31,054 --> 00:33:32,472
Why should I have to take

406
00:33:33,140 --> 00:33:34,683
that kind of criticism
because of you?

407
00:33:37,060 --> 00:33:38,061
Ah-jin.

408
00:33:43,191 --> 00:33:44,568
Let me ask you one favor.

409
00:33:46,236 --> 00:33:49,656
You're a good guy who always
does me a favor when I ask

410
00:33:49,906 --> 00:33:52,200
so I hope you do it again this time.

411
00:33:56,496 --> 00:33:58,373
Let's break up.

412
00:34:07,466 --> 00:34:08,717
Hang on.

413
00:34:09,384 --> 00:34:11,303
What kind of nonsense is this?

414
00:34:11,386 --> 00:34:13,221
This is too sudden.

415
00:34:14,473 --> 00:34:15,932
I know you're angry, but...

416
00:34:17,768 --> 00:34:19,644
Are you even the same Ah-jin I know?

417
00:34:19,728 --> 00:34:23,231
And are you the In-gang I know?

418
00:34:24,524 --> 00:34:26,401
You're not in your right mind.

419
00:34:27,152 --> 00:34:28,820
You can't even control your emotions

420
00:34:28,904 --> 00:34:30,989
babbling about retiring
and fairy-tale dreams.

421
00:34:31,073 --> 00:34:32,783
Get a grip.

422
00:34:33,617 --> 00:34:37,537
Do you know how many fans you've lost
in the year we've been together?

423
00:34:37,788 --> 00:34:39,998
And now you want me to marry you?

424
00:34:42,250 --> 00:34:44,961
Don't make me laugh.
And what about me?

425
00:34:46,296 --> 00:34:48,507
You want to put
a "married woman" label on me

426
00:34:48,590 --> 00:34:51,843
while I lose my movie roles,
so I can watch as my career dies?

427
00:34:53,845 --> 00:34:57,516
How can a person change
so completely overnight?

428
00:34:58,767 --> 00:34:59,768
Why?

429
00:35:02,521 --> 00:35:04,314
You don't like the new me?

430
00:35:05,732 --> 00:35:08,777
Then would you rather have me
smile sweetly

431
00:35:10,153 --> 00:35:11,696
while I break up with you?

432
00:35:13,532 --> 00:35:15,242
Would that make it easier for you?

433
00:35:20,497 --> 00:35:21,957
We've been together a year.

434
00:35:23,875 --> 00:35:27,087
I thought I knew you,
and I was certain about us.

435
00:35:28,588 --> 00:35:30,715
That's why I pictured
a future together.

436
00:35:31,842 --> 00:35:33,301
Was that so wrong?

437
00:35:34,094 --> 00:35:36,096
You know how much pain
I'm in right now.

438
00:35:37,472 --> 00:35:38,640
Can't you even try to understand--

439
00:35:38,723 --> 00:35:41,059
Why should I understand you?

440
00:35:42,394 --> 00:35:44,312
It wasn't ten years,
not even five years.

441
00:35:44,396 --> 00:35:47,232
Who cares
about a one-year relationship?

442
00:35:47,858 --> 00:35:50,402
You thought I knew you? Well, I...

443
00:35:52,863 --> 00:35:55,365
I've never heard
such an arrogant thing in my life.

444
00:36:00,287 --> 00:36:01,955
I can't believe this.

445
00:36:04,040 --> 00:36:05,667
I wish this were a dream.

446
00:36:07,252 --> 00:36:09,129
Given your tragic life

447
00:36:09,212 --> 00:36:10,922
I'm probably not
even nightmare-worthy.

448
00:36:13,216 --> 00:36:16,136
Don't make a scene over something
as ordinary as a breakup.

449
00:36:23,143 --> 00:36:24,352
Ah-jin, what's wrong?

450
00:36:24,436 --> 00:36:25,478
Come on.

451
00:36:27,564 --> 00:36:29,399
- Don't do this.
- In-gang.

452
00:36:32,736 --> 00:36:33,862
What I'm about to say

453
00:36:35,030 --> 00:36:36,239
will hurt.

454
00:36:43,705 --> 00:36:45,332
I'm already hurting.

455
00:36:48,960 --> 00:36:50,503
You were pretending ignorance.

456
00:37:06,269 --> 00:37:07,395
But listen anyway.

457
00:37:08,772 --> 00:37:09,940
Don't try to avoid it.

458
00:37:15,946 --> 00:37:17,155
Your grandma's notebook.

459
00:37:19,616 --> 00:37:20,909
I stole it.

460
00:37:24,329 --> 00:37:27,707
I wanted to win her favor
so I could date you.

461
00:37:29,793 --> 00:37:33,046
She found it at my place a while ago

462
00:37:34,256 --> 00:37:35,465
and she found out...

463
00:37:37,300 --> 00:37:38,677
what kind of person I am.

464
00:37:40,929 --> 00:37:42,055
And from that shock

465
00:37:43,306 --> 00:37:44,307
she...

466
00:37:49,020 --> 00:37:50,730
You understand what I mean, right?

467
00:37:57,988 --> 00:37:58,989
In-gang.

468
00:38:01,283 --> 00:38:02,284
How you fell

469
00:38:04,244 --> 00:38:06,204
in love with me...

470
00:38:08,623 --> 00:38:10,292
and what happened to your grandma--

471
00:38:10,375 --> 00:38:11,668
What the hell did you do?

472
00:38:14,129 --> 00:38:15,130
All I did was...

473
00:38:17,882 --> 00:38:19,843
tell her the truth.

474
00:38:22,304 --> 00:38:24,973
I asked what you did to my grandma!

475
00:38:31,646 --> 00:38:33,398
I simply told her honestly.

476
00:38:34,858 --> 00:38:37,527
For once in my life.

477
00:38:56,504 --> 00:38:57,672
Say that again.

478
00:39:02,093 --> 00:39:03,595
If you don't let go of me now

479
00:39:04,512 --> 00:39:07,098
you'll be in hell
every time you think of her.

480
00:39:08,308 --> 00:39:10,852
You're not the type of person
who can handle that.

481
00:39:14,356 --> 00:39:15,440
So, admit it.

482
00:39:16,733 --> 00:39:18,902
Our ending was already decided.

483
00:39:23,073 --> 00:39:24,949
I'll release the breakup article

484
00:39:25,033 --> 00:39:28,411
through a reporter I know
at the right time.

485
00:39:29,287 --> 00:39:34,292
The reason will be
"grew apart due to busy schedules."

486
00:39:35,794 --> 00:39:37,128
About Ms. Seo...

487
00:39:39,672 --> 00:39:41,633
I'll tell her myself,
so get some rest for now.

488
00:39:43,426 --> 00:39:45,553
You look like you haven't slept
since your grandma passed.

489
00:39:48,807 --> 00:39:49,808
Get a good sleep.

490
00:40:36,521 --> 00:40:38,064
It's me, Mr. Lim.

491
00:40:38,148 --> 00:40:40,024
What is it, at this hour?

492
00:40:40,108 --> 00:40:42,527
I think it's time to end
our little arrangement.

493
00:40:43,236 --> 00:40:44,237
What?

494
00:40:44,487 --> 00:40:46,614
Don't tell me
you're going to marry In-gang.

495
00:40:46,698 --> 00:40:48,074
No, it's the opposite.

496
00:40:48,158 --> 00:40:49,159
The opposite?

497
00:40:49,242 --> 00:40:51,494
Get a breakup article ready for us.

498
00:40:51,578 --> 00:40:53,288
Breakup? Hold on.

499
00:40:53,371 --> 00:40:56,416
Just write we drifted apart
due to our busy schedules.

500
00:40:56,499 --> 00:40:59,210
- You're seriously going through--
- As quickly as possible, please.

501
00:41:02,046 --> 00:41:04,924
CEO SEO MI-RI

502
00:41:17,270 --> 00:41:18,313
Hey, Boss.

503
00:41:18,396 --> 00:41:19,397
Where are you?

504
00:41:34,829 --> 00:41:37,040
Boss, don't pull over.
Just keep driving.

505
00:41:37,123 --> 00:41:38,416
You've got a tail behind you.

506
00:42:14,869 --> 00:42:16,079
Who are you?

507
00:42:16,371 --> 00:42:18,248
Are you a stalker?

508
00:42:18,540 --> 00:42:19,541
Or gangsters?

509
00:42:20,083 --> 00:42:21,960
You've got nothing better
to do with your lives?

510
00:42:23,586 --> 00:42:24,587
Get out.

511
00:42:45,316 --> 00:42:46,317
Get him.

512
00:42:47,026 --> 00:42:48,736
- No!
- Punk.

513
00:43:08,840 --> 00:43:09,882
Let's stop all this.

514
00:43:10,133 --> 00:43:12,010
Forget about Ah-jin now.

515
00:43:25,398 --> 00:43:27,567
She's not the right girl for you.

516
00:43:27,650 --> 00:43:29,110
We won't renew her contract, either.

517
00:43:29,902 --> 00:43:31,070
I know.

518
00:43:33,197 --> 00:43:36,075
All lovers break up in the end.

519
00:43:39,245 --> 00:43:41,205
This kind of breakup happens
to everybody.

520
00:43:43,708 --> 00:43:44,959
Just today.

521
00:43:46,669 --> 00:43:48,880
I'll let it hurt just for today.

522
00:43:54,636 --> 00:43:55,845
Just for today?

523
00:44:03,645 --> 00:44:05,980
Fine. Let's drink, then.

524
00:44:09,859 --> 00:44:11,611
Let's get totally wasted tonight.

525
00:44:15,740 --> 00:44:17,367
It brings back old memories.

526
00:44:23,414 --> 00:44:24,457
Thanks, Mi-ri.

527
00:44:26,000 --> 00:44:27,001
For what?

528
00:44:31,881 --> 00:44:32,882
Thank you.

529
00:44:36,177 --> 00:44:37,178
Silly.

530
00:44:37,762 --> 00:44:39,180
Pour me some more. Is this a joke?

531
00:45:05,248 --> 00:45:06,249
AH-JIN

532
00:45:18,636 --> 00:45:19,846
Hey, Ah-jin.

533
00:45:20,346 --> 00:45:22,849
Jae-oh, who was in that car
that was following me?

534
00:45:25,309 --> 00:45:26,310
Paparazzi.

535
00:45:27,562 --> 00:45:29,439
I talked to them and sent them away

536
00:45:30,189 --> 00:45:31,190
so don't worry.

537
00:45:33,526 --> 00:45:36,070
You didn't call me out
for something urgent, right?

538
00:45:36,904 --> 00:45:40,283
No, I'm a little tired today.
I'll talk to you later.

539
00:45:42,493 --> 00:45:43,870
I'll call you.

540
00:46:21,240 --> 00:46:22,325
What?

541
00:46:22,408 --> 00:46:24,035
HEO IN-GANG AND BAEK AH-JIN
BREAK UP AFTER 1 YEAR

542
00:46:24,118 --> 00:46:25,411
GREW DISTANT DUE TO BUSY SCHEDULES

543
00:46:25,495 --> 00:46:26,996
THE FAMOUS COUPLE
HEO IN-GANG AND BAEK AH-JIN

544
00:46:27,079 --> 00:46:28,623
ENDED THEIR RELATIONSHIP
AFTER A TURBULENT YEAR

545
00:46:36,589 --> 00:46:38,257
Ms. Seo, these documents are for you.

546
00:46:39,175 --> 00:46:41,010
Yes, fix the parts I marked.

547
00:46:42,261 --> 00:46:43,346
Where's In-gang?

548
00:46:43,596 --> 00:46:44,847
His manager called and said

549
00:46:44,931 --> 00:46:46,849
he just went to bed
after taking sleeping pills.

550
00:46:48,476 --> 00:46:50,311
He won't be up
until late afternoon, then.

551
00:46:50,895 --> 00:46:52,104
That brat probably skipped food

552
00:46:52,188 --> 00:46:53,731
and poured alcohol
into an empty stomach.

553
00:46:56,025 --> 00:46:58,194
Is there
a good hangover-soup place nearby?

554
00:46:58,945 --> 00:47:00,446
Are you taking it to him?

555
00:47:00,530 --> 00:47:02,573
I'll swing by his place
on my way home.

556
00:47:03,366 --> 00:47:06,953
I need to make him eat something
and pull himself together.

557
00:47:39,569 --> 00:47:41,487
I'm out of town right now

558
00:47:41,571 --> 00:47:43,239
but In-gang isn't picking up
the phone.

559
00:47:43,698 --> 00:47:46,075
He's just passed out
from drinking too much.

560
00:47:46,158 --> 00:47:47,660
I'm heading over
with hangover soup now.

561
00:47:47,743 --> 00:47:50,329
I'll feed him
and tell him to call you.

562
00:47:50,413 --> 00:47:51,414
Yes.

563
00:47:51,497 --> 00:47:53,165
Don't worry, In-mo.
Focus on your work.

564
00:47:53,249 --> 00:47:54,375
Okay.

565
00:48:17,481 --> 00:48:20,067
In-gang, wake up!
Time to fix that hangover.

566
00:48:21,277 --> 00:48:25,156
I brought you
some amazing hangover soup.

567
00:48:32,079 --> 00:48:34,373
He's still asleep, huh?

568
00:48:36,626 --> 00:48:37,835
In-gang!

569
00:48:41,589 --> 00:48:43,591
Where is he?

570
00:50:20,896 --> 00:50:21,897
In-gang.

571
00:50:23,983 --> 00:50:25,317
In-gang, no.

572
00:50:27,445 --> 00:50:29,572
No!

573
00:50:30,990 --> 00:50:33,409
No!

574
00:51:11,113 --> 00:51:12,114
Hey.

575
00:51:12,948 --> 00:51:14,241
Look at me.

576
00:51:15,284 --> 00:51:16,285
Ridiculous, right?

577
00:51:21,373 --> 00:51:22,374
What happened?

578
00:51:22,958 --> 00:51:24,376
You've never been this hurt.

579
00:51:24,877 --> 00:51:26,003
What have you been doing?

580
00:51:28,380 --> 00:51:31,217
I just got unlucky.

581
00:51:33,219 --> 00:51:34,220
How's Boss?

582
00:51:35,554 --> 00:51:36,555
What?

583
00:51:36,972 --> 00:51:38,015
Is she all right?

584
00:51:38,516 --> 00:51:39,642
Why are you asking that?

585
00:51:42,228 --> 00:51:43,938
As long as nothing happened to her.

586
00:51:55,533 --> 00:51:57,243
Who the hell were those guys, anyway?

587
00:51:57,326 --> 00:51:58,869
Heo In-gang is dead.

588
00:52:00,121 --> 00:52:01,497
Seriously? Was it suicide?

589
00:52:01,997 --> 00:52:04,250
But he recently broke up
with Baek Ah-jin.

590
00:52:04,333 --> 00:52:07,253
Wait, does that mean
he killed himself because of her?

591
00:52:07,336 --> 00:52:08,712
That can't be.

592
00:52:08,796 --> 00:52:10,089
Apparently, he had depression.

593
00:52:45,416 --> 00:52:47,251
What did you say to me before?

594
00:52:47,501 --> 00:52:49,295
What did you say to me last time?

595
00:52:51,130 --> 00:52:53,591
You said you were just going to have
a normal relationship and break up.

596
00:52:53,674 --> 00:52:56,093
You said yourself
that he wouldn't get hurt.

597
00:52:56,886 --> 00:52:58,137
You're hilarious.

598
00:52:58,762 --> 00:52:59,763
Why are you angry?

599
00:53:01,390 --> 00:53:03,184
Who are you to yell at me?

600
00:53:05,019 --> 00:53:07,229
He couldn't accept the breakup.
That's on him.

601
00:53:07,313 --> 00:53:08,981
I did everything I could.

602
00:53:09,607 --> 00:53:11,025
How is that my fault?

603
00:53:11,692 --> 00:53:14,820
It was bad luck on his part
that he ended up like that.

604
00:53:16,530 --> 00:53:17,948
That's not my fault.

605
00:53:23,204 --> 00:53:24,580
He's dead.

606
00:53:26,040 --> 00:53:28,584
An entire family was shattered
in an instant.

607
00:53:31,212 --> 00:53:32,630
And that's all you have to say?

608
00:53:33,714 --> 00:53:36,300
You make it sound like I killed him.

609
00:53:36,383 --> 00:53:37,426
Didn't you?

610
00:53:39,595 --> 00:53:42,389
Did you think I'd feel guilty?

611
00:53:42,473 --> 00:53:44,058
Don't expect that from me.

612
00:53:44,642 --> 00:53:46,518
You're the only one
who'll end up hurt and disappointed.

613
00:53:52,858 --> 00:53:53,901
Can't you just...

614
00:53:55,736 --> 00:53:57,446
live like a normal person?

615
00:54:02,910 --> 00:54:04,870
It was my mistake
for thinking you had

616
00:54:04,954 --> 00:54:06,789
even a shred of humanity in you.

617
00:54:08,374 --> 00:54:10,626
How exactly
am I supposed to be human?

618
00:54:11,502 --> 00:54:14,255
Do you think things would have
turned out differently

619
00:54:14,338 --> 00:54:16,257
if you had pulled me
out of that bathtub?

620
00:54:17,299 --> 00:54:19,009
But you didn't.

621
00:54:19,093 --> 00:54:21,428
Jae-oh would have stormed
into the bathroom

622
00:54:21,512 --> 00:54:24,223
and smashed that woman's head,
but you didn't.

623
00:54:24,765 --> 00:54:27,017
And you dare to judge me?

624
00:54:30,854 --> 00:54:34,149
Did you just stand there and watch
because you had humanity?

625
00:54:36,193 --> 00:54:37,945
This isn't my fault.

626
00:54:38,988 --> 00:54:40,823
You made me like this.

627
00:54:43,534 --> 00:54:46,537
If you feel bad for me,
say you're sorry.

628
00:54:47,621 --> 00:54:50,291
Say you're sorry
you turned me into this.

629
00:54:51,792 --> 00:54:53,377
When you condemn me

630
00:54:53,460 --> 00:54:55,170
you're actually condemning
your past self.

631
00:55:05,347 --> 00:55:07,224
You can blame me all you want

632
00:55:08,642 --> 00:55:10,269
but I'll never blame you.

633
00:55:20,070 --> 00:55:22,990
If you want to leave me, then do it.

634
00:55:27,411 --> 00:55:29,455
Run away from me

635
00:55:29,955 --> 00:55:31,582
just like you did in the past...

636
00:55:33,625 --> 00:55:35,961
and I still won't blame you.

637
00:55:42,092 --> 00:55:45,012
Because you're the first person
I chose to keep by my side.

638
00:56:25,719 --> 00:56:28,806
I was afraid my grandma
wouldn't be able to get her surgery.

639
00:56:29,765 --> 00:56:31,392
Thank you, Manager.

640
00:56:32,059 --> 00:56:33,519
I'll never forget this.

641
00:56:33,602 --> 00:56:35,229
I'm not a manager anymore.

642
00:56:35,312 --> 00:56:37,856
You can call me CEO now.

643
00:56:37,940 --> 00:56:39,066
And just so you know

644
00:56:39,149 --> 00:56:41,276
I never forget
a favor I gave, either.

645
00:56:41,360 --> 00:56:42,569
Thank you, truly.

646
00:56:45,114 --> 00:56:46,115
Hello.

647
00:56:51,745 --> 00:56:53,497
You said you never forget
a favor you've done.

648
00:56:53,747 --> 00:56:55,416
I wish you massive success, Ms. Seo.

649
00:56:57,042 --> 00:56:58,335
Thank you.

650
00:56:59,920 --> 00:57:02,131
REPRESENTATIVE: SEO MI-RI
NAME: HEO IN-GANG

651
00:57:05,801 --> 00:57:07,719
I never forget
the favors I receive, either.

652
00:57:08,137 --> 00:57:09,680
I sure know
how to pick the right people.

653
00:57:17,980 --> 00:57:21,191
I just want to thank you.

654
00:57:36,582 --> 00:57:39,168
HEO IN-GANG

655
00:58:50,489 --> 00:58:52,241
Everyone ends up abandoned

656
00:58:52,908 --> 00:58:54,159
and broken in life.

657
00:58:55,452 --> 00:58:57,329
You were just too weak.

658
00:59:08,674 --> 00:59:10,842
I couldn't just fall apart with you.

659
00:59:21,061 --> 00:59:22,437
Please understand me.

660
00:59:55,012 --> 00:59:56,847
- Kick her out!
- Kick her out!

661
00:59:56,930 --> 00:59:58,515
Kick Baek Ah-jin out!

662
00:59:58,599 --> 01:00:00,350
- Kick her out!
- Kick her out!

663
01:00:00,434 --> 01:00:01,852
This is unfair!

664
01:00:01,935 --> 01:00:03,729
- Unfair!
- Unfair!

665
01:00:03,812 --> 01:00:05,606
Take responsibility, Longstar!

666
01:00:05,689 --> 01:00:07,524
- Take responsibility!
- Take responsibility!

667
01:00:07,608 --> 01:00:09,234
This is unfair!

668
01:00:09,318 --> 01:00:11,236
- Unfair!
- Unfair!

669
01:00:11,320 --> 01:00:13,113
Baek Ah-jin is a criminal!

670
01:00:13,196 --> 01:00:15,073
- Criminal!
- Criminal!

671
01:00:15,157 --> 01:00:16,867
Kick Baek Ah-jin out!

672
01:00:16,950 --> 01:00:18,869
- Kick her out!
- Kick her out!

673
01:00:18,952 --> 01:00:20,579
Bring In-gang back!

674
01:00:20,662 --> 01:00:22,331
- Bring him back!
- Bring him back!

675
01:00:22,414 --> 01:00:24,499
Take responsibility, Longstar!

676
01:00:24,583 --> 01:00:26,585
- Take responsibility!
- Take responsibility!

677
01:00:26,668 --> 01:00:28,378
Bring In-gang back!

678
01:00:28,462 --> 01:00:30,380
- Bring him back!
- Bring him back!

679
01:00:30,464 --> 01:00:31,465
Baek Ah-jin!

680
01:00:32,716 --> 01:00:35,010
- Bring him back.
- Bring In-gang back.

681
01:00:35,761 --> 01:00:37,679
- Devil!
- You're the worst!

682
01:00:38,388 --> 01:00:39,931
Who are you? Move!

683
01:00:40,515 --> 01:00:42,851
I was her classmate.

684
01:00:42,934 --> 01:00:44,728
She doesn't deserve all this insult!

685
01:00:44,811 --> 01:00:46,855
- Where do you think you're going?
- Go away!

686
01:00:46,938 --> 01:00:49,441
- Come back here!
- Baek Ah-jin!

687
01:00:49,524 --> 01:00:52,152
- You're a devil!
- Bring him back to life!

688
01:00:53,111 --> 01:00:56,156
- Stop!
- Bring In-gang back!

689
01:00:56,448 --> 01:00:57,949
- Get away from her!
- Come here!

690
01:00:59,076 --> 01:01:00,786
Who the heck is she?

691
01:01:06,166 --> 01:01:09,252
Hey, I'm all filthy because of you,
so let me wash up first.

692
01:01:10,420 --> 01:01:11,963
Seriously.

693
01:01:12,798 --> 01:01:13,799
Hey.

694
01:01:19,054 --> 01:01:21,348
You have a nice place.

695
01:01:41,993 --> 01:01:43,662
So fancy.

696
01:01:44,663 --> 01:01:45,664
This is insane.

697
01:01:49,084 --> 01:01:51,044
You have lots of nice clothes.

698
01:01:53,964 --> 01:01:55,173
I missed you.

699
01:01:56,049 --> 01:01:57,926
Not bad for an orphan.

700
01:01:59,720 --> 01:02:01,304
You're successful now.

701
01:02:01,388 --> 01:02:02,681
Impressive, friend.

702
01:02:08,562 --> 01:02:11,606
Bring me some booze.
You drink, right?

703
01:02:12,566 --> 01:02:13,567
Right?

704
01:02:18,613 --> 01:02:19,656
Get out of my house.

705
01:02:23,326 --> 01:02:25,370
You used to run loan-shark schemes
on kids back in school

706
01:02:25,454 --> 01:02:27,497
and now look at you.

707
01:02:30,709 --> 01:02:32,419
Let me try that scheme, too.

708
01:02:33,962 --> 01:02:35,172
How about 100,000 won a day?

709
01:02:40,635 --> 01:02:43,513
Don't pick fights you can't win,
and get out.

710
01:02:47,476 --> 01:02:48,477
Fine.

711
01:02:49,060 --> 01:02:50,061
For now...

712
01:02:53,440 --> 01:02:55,066
I'll take this and call it even.

713
01:03:02,783 --> 01:03:04,493
The public sentiment
is extremely negative.

714
01:03:04,576 --> 01:03:07,329
Longstar also hasn't made
a clear statement yet

715
01:03:07,412 --> 01:03:09,456
so speculative articles
are flooding in.

716
01:03:11,249 --> 01:03:15,086
The agency's actor is under attack,
and they're merely watching?

717
01:03:27,682 --> 01:03:29,976
I know you were digging
into Ah-jin's father's death

718
01:03:30,060 --> 01:03:32,312
and stopped
when you started working with her.

719
01:03:34,439 --> 01:03:36,441
I suggest you work with me now.

720
01:03:39,611 --> 01:03:41,905
We may not be able
to reopen the whole case

721
01:03:41,988 --> 01:03:43,824
but this will be enough
to drag her down

722
01:03:43,907 --> 01:03:45,617
since she lives off public image.

723
01:03:46,910 --> 01:03:48,119
Is this everything?

724
01:03:48,203 --> 01:03:49,412
Just a portion.

725
01:03:50,372 --> 01:03:53,458
I'll give you the rest
as soon as you agree.

726
01:03:54,000 --> 01:03:56,419
Think about it and get back to me.

727
01:03:57,671 --> 01:03:58,880
Ms. Seo.

728
01:04:00,382 --> 01:04:02,300
You do know timing is everything
with exposés, right?

729
01:04:02,384 --> 01:04:03,552
About that timing...

730
01:04:04,886 --> 01:04:07,138
The sooner, the better.

731
01:04:45,135 --> 01:04:46,261
What are you doing?

732
01:04:47,596 --> 01:04:48,597
I'm sorry.

733
01:04:50,307 --> 01:04:51,308
Ah-jin.

734
01:04:52,767 --> 01:04:54,477
Is this a new persona
you're trying out?

735
01:04:57,731 --> 01:04:59,232
Sorry about what, exactly?

736
01:05:00,567 --> 01:05:03,028
I truly want to apologize.

737
01:05:06,698 --> 01:05:08,158
For everything I've done...

738
01:05:10,744 --> 01:05:11,912
I'm sorry.

739
01:05:13,747 --> 01:05:14,748
Ah-jin.

740
01:05:16,625 --> 01:05:17,626
After all this time?

741
01:05:29,220 --> 01:05:31,097
I'm even on my knees.

742
01:05:34,142 --> 01:05:37,228
Won't you please accept my apology?

743
01:05:38,647 --> 01:05:39,648
Please?

744
01:05:53,411 --> 01:05:54,412
Why should I?

745
01:05:55,997 --> 01:05:58,541
Why should I accept your apology?

746
01:06:02,212 --> 01:06:03,213
Ms. Hwang.

747
01:06:03,838 --> 01:06:05,340
For kneeling once?

748
01:06:07,175 --> 01:06:09,135
Considering everything
you've done to me

749
01:06:09,219 --> 01:06:11,721
your knees should be
worn down to the bones.

750
01:06:16,559 --> 01:06:18,228
Deep down, you've been waiting

751
01:06:19,396 --> 01:06:20,647
for my apology.

752
01:06:26,444 --> 01:06:27,612
I don't need it.

753
01:06:30,782 --> 01:06:31,783
Is that right?

754
01:06:37,163 --> 01:06:38,748
Well, I apologized.

755
01:06:45,296 --> 01:06:47,173
Don't forget to tell Jun-seo

756
01:06:48,133 --> 01:06:50,552
that I came and apologized.

757
01:06:53,513 --> 01:06:55,306
Make sure he knows

758
01:06:56,391 --> 01:06:57,517
I got on my knees.

759
01:08:38,827 --> 01:08:39,828
Do you know...

760
01:08:44,082 --> 01:08:46,876
when I hated you the most?

761
01:09:12,819 --> 01:09:15,405
I asked what you did to my grandma!

762
01:09:17,240 --> 01:09:18,366
I admit

763
01:09:19,325 --> 01:09:22,328
that was my intention at first.

764
01:09:24,789 --> 01:09:26,040
But...

765
01:09:32,130 --> 01:09:33,548
I liked

766
01:09:34,841 --> 01:09:36,259
In-gang so much.

767
01:09:40,096 --> 01:09:41,306
So, I...

768
01:09:44,767 --> 01:09:48,354
wanted you to love me, too.

769
01:09:58,323 --> 01:10:00,408
I'll take care of it.

770
01:10:06,623 --> 01:10:08,416
I'll tell

771
01:10:10,293 --> 01:10:12,503
In-gang the truth...

772
01:10:16,174 --> 01:10:17,508
and end this.

773
01:10:25,850 --> 01:10:27,101
Look at me.

774
01:10:40,240 --> 01:10:42,158
I still stand by it.

775
01:10:46,037 --> 01:10:47,038
The fact

776
01:10:48,623 --> 01:10:50,458
that you're also one of my children

777
01:10:51,918 --> 01:10:54,003
just like In-gang and In-mo.

778
01:10:56,047 --> 01:10:58,716
When your child does wrong,
you scold them

779
01:10:59,676 --> 01:11:01,261
and embrace them again.

780
01:11:03,805 --> 01:11:05,265
That's what a parent does.

781
01:11:21,030 --> 01:11:22,282
Ah-jin.

782
01:11:23,616 --> 01:11:24,826
Baek Ah-jin.

783
01:11:26,744 --> 01:11:27,745
Yes?

784
01:11:28,830 --> 01:11:30,290
You did wrong, didn't you?

785
01:11:36,421 --> 01:11:38,172
You won't do it again, right?

786
01:11:44,762 --> 01:11:46,180
That's good enough.

787
01:11:49,267 --> 01:11:50,268
Ah-jin.

788
01:11:52,186 --> 01:11:53,980
Here's what we should do.

789
01:11:55,648 --> 01:11:59,485
We'll keep this just between us

790
01:12:00,403 --> 01:12:01,612
and never tell anyone.

791
01:12:11,497 --> 01:12:14,500
My other babies must have arrived.

792
01:12:21,799 --> 01:12:23,468
Do you want to meet them?

793
01:12:32,602 --> 01:12:33,686
I hated you the most

794
01:12:36,064 --> 01:12:38,483
when you were kind to me
every once in a while.

795
01:12:49,035 --> 01:12:51,162
Because I would be tricked
by your kindness

796
01:12:53,206 --> 01:12:55,458
and start to fall for it.

797
01:13:02,173 --> 01:13:04,842
I was afraid of having
even a tiny bit of false hope.

798
01:13:10,598 --> 01:13:12,016
That's what scared me.

799
01:14:09,866 --> 01:14:11,909
Come on. Come.

800
01:16:57,825 --> 01:16:59,452
But now I know for sure.

801
01:17:22,433 --> 01:17:24,727
It's all my fault.

802
01:17:27,271 --> 01:17:28,606
Save her life.

803
01:17:33,444 --> 01:17:35,321
Please save her life.

804
01:17:36,280 --> 01:17:37,865
In hell, hope is...

805
01:17:42,703 --> 01:17:44,580
something you should never hold onto.

806
01:18:49,353 --> 01:18:51,480
They don't seem to know
who we are yet.

807
01:18:51,564 --> 01:18:53,441
It looks like he followed us
by coincidence.

808
01:18:53,524 --> 01:18:55,818
She's hospitalized at the moment.

809
01:18:56,485 --> 01:18:57,653
What would you have me do?

810
01:19:01,115 --> 01:19:02,241
Let's observe for now.

811
01:19:03,576 --> 01:19:07,121
Find out exactly
how they're connected.

812
01:19:07,204 --> 01:19:08,205
Yes, sir.

813
01:20:24,406 --> 01:20:28,744
DEAR X

814
01:22:48,258 --> 01:22:50,260
Subtitles by Ho-young Yun

